blofanpinga'a = blo (bloti=boat) + fan (falnu=sail) + pin (pinta=horizontal)
+ ga'a(grana=pole)

Although maybe it would be better for the {pin} to precede {fan}.

Anyway, the sail is held by two poles - the mast, which is vertical, and the
boom, which is horizontal. The mast is talked about more often, so it gets
{blofanga'a}, whereas the boom is horizontal.

It works great in speech too:
  .i blofanpinga'a
meaning: we've just made an uncontrolled jibe, so the boom is swinging right
at your head. Duck!

